            .docNews: "1.5.2 — 2026-07-28\n\n• windows in the dock — the converter, archives, recognition and the rest show up in the dock while they are open, so a click brings the window back without opening the panel first\n\n• memory — the row now warns when a lot of your memory has gone to disk, not only when macOS says it is struggling; the threshold is in monitor settings\n\n• links in qr codes — frame a code on a bill and the link inside it opens in your browser, no phone needed\n\n• four new languages — Arabic, Hebrew, Persian and Urdu; as always, the app picks up your system language on its own\n\n• right to left — choose one of them and the whole panel mirrors, with the text set in a face that keeps the script joined\n\n• fix — the empty torrent row stays hidden once you have hidden it, an update no longer brings it back\n\n1.5.1 — 2026-07-27\n\n• file archives — Hop now asks only for rar — everything else stays with the system's own Archive Utility, and settings can hand back what an older version took. an archive opened from Finder unpacks right beside itself, in a small progress window, and a failed one leaves nothing hidden\n\n• file icons — every file Hop opens carries its own icon with the format written across it, so a folder of them tells you what is what\n\n• monitor — the memory figure matches Activity Monitor exactly, and the temperature colour follows the system's own verdict on heat instead of a fixed number\n\n• fixes — a finished torrent now says what it downloaded and whether it is still sharing, the keyboard lock releases the moment you ask, and hop can be installed with homebrew\n\n1.5.0 — 2026-07-26\n\n• file archives — drop a zip, rar, 7z or tar.gz and it unpacks beside the original; drop files and they become one archive there. Hop can also be the opener for archives in Finder\n\n• cleaning mode — one tap locks the whole keyboard so it can be wiped: 1, 5, 15 minutes or until you say stop. the mouse, the panel or holding esc releases it\n\n• color picker — pick any color on screen and keep it as a list, each one carrying hex, rgb and hsl to copy with a click\n\n• text recognition — frame an area of the screen, or drop and paste a picture: the text and qr codes inside it come out in a window and go to the clipboard history\n\n• documents in the converter — markdown, word files and pdfs turned into one another, a pdf's text pulled out as markdown, all on this Mac\n\n• permissions — a tab in this window listing every permission Hop can ask for, what it is for, whether it is granted, and what Hop never does\n\n1.4.0 — 2026-07-22\n\n• tabs — the icon holds up to four of them now, and modules drag freely between them\n\n• time tracker — a new module: time per task, today and in total, with a nudge past 8 hours\n\n• to-do list — a new module: a short list of tasks right in the panel\n\n• copied files — the clipboard remembers a file by name, and pasting drops the file itself back\n\n• icon indicators — small status marks on the menu-bar icon, colored or monochrome\n\n• supporting hop — for anyone who would like to, there is now a way\n\n1.3.1 — 2026-07-18\n\n• torrents — enabling the module downloads the engine right away, with live progress and follow-up choices in the card\n\n• monitor — memory, disk and network figures now match Activity Monitor and Finder exactly\n\n• download icon — it lights up only while a torrent is actually downloading",
