            .permPledgeTitle: "every permission here exists so a feature can work — and for nothing else.",
            .permPledgeBody: "Hop has no server, no analytics, no telemetry, no account and no crash reports. Nothing about you is collected, and nothing leaves this Mac — not now, not in a later version. You do not have to take that on trust: the whole app is open source, so the code that would have to do the collecting simply is not there.",
            .permPledgeLink: "read the source on GitHub",
            .showInPanel: "show in the panel",
            .docKeylockFull: "cleaning mode: one tap and the whole keyboard stops responding, so it can be wiped without shutting the Mac down or closing the lid.\n\n• {sym:keyboard} how it starts — the module has no start button: tapping a length starts it. 1, 5 or 15 minutes, or ∞ to stay locked until you say otherwise.\n\n• while it is on — a full-screen cover explains what is happening, and the menu-bar star turns into a keyboard so the reason the keys are dead is visible at a glance. every press, release and modifier is swallowed, including the brightness, volume and media row. nothing is recorded: the events are dropped, never read.\n\n• four ways out — none of them a shortcut: the done button on the cover, the unlock button in the panel, simply opening Hop's panel, or holding esc + shift for five seconds if the mouse is out of reach. unlocking plays a short cue.\n\n• the power button — a short press is swallowed like everything else, but holding it still forces the Mac off: that is handled in hardware and never reaches an app. Touch ID keeps working too.\n\n• accessibility permission — the same one the window manager uses, because swallowing keys system-wide is exactly what it governs. without it the keys would keep firing, so Hop asks before promising a lock.",
            .featureModulesTitle: "new modules",
            .featureModulesBody: "tick the modules you want to see in the panel right away.",
            .featureModulesConverter: "the converter also takes md files now — into pdf and docx.",
            .permTab: "app permissions", .permGranted: "granted", .permNotGranted: "not granted",
            .permWhenUsed: "asked when used", .permNetworkTitle: "network — antonshakirov.com",
            .permNetworkBody: "checking for updates and downloading them, plus the two optional helpers: the torrent engine and the 7-Zip archiver. that is the only server Hop talks to on its own.",
            .permTorrentTitle: "network — torrent traffic",
            .permTorrentBody: "only with the torrent module on: connections to other peers, exactly like any torrent client. nothing passes through us.",
            .permSpeedTitle: "network — speed test",
            .permSpeedBody: "the speed test runs macOS's own networkQuality tool, which measures against Apple's servers. no third-party service is involved.",
            .permAccessibilityTitle: "accessibility",
            .permAccessibilityBody: "three things need it: pasting into the app underneath (the clipboard's paste button), moving and resizing windows, and the keyboard lock. macOS governs all of them with this one switch.",
            .permScreenTitle: "screen recording",
            .permScreenBody: "only the text recognition module, and only when it frames an area on screen: a frame means reading its pixels. a dropped or pasted picture needs nothing at all. Hop reads the rectangle you draw, when you ask for it, and nothing else. the eyedropper does NOT need this — the system loupe hands back a single color.",
            .permNotifyTitle: "notifications",
            .permNotifyBody: "the timer's alert when it finishes, and a note when a torrent completes. nothing else is ever posted.",
            .permAdminTitle: "administrator password",
            .permAdminBody: "asked once, by macOS itself, only for the closed-lid mode: keeping the Mac awake with the lid shut needs pmset, which is root-only. no background daemon is installed.",
            .permLoginTitle: "launch at login",
            .permLoginBody: "off unless you turn it on, in settings. it registers Hop with macOS's own login-items service — no scripts, no plists left behind.",
            .permNeverTitle: "what Hop never does",
            .permNeverBody: "no analytics, no telemetry, no account, no crash reports sent anywhere. the clipboard history, the tracker and the to-do list live only on this Mac. files are touched only when you drop them on Hop or pick them yourself, and no permission is requested until the feature that needs it is actually used.",
