            .visibleRowsLabel: "visible rows",
            .aboutTabTasks: "tasks & time",
            .docTrackerFull: "time tracker — a flat list of tasks, each with an all-time total that ticks up while the task runs. only one task runs at a time.\n\n• start / stop — the round button on the left starts a task; starting another stops the first. the total climbs live while a task is active.\n\n• rename — double-click a task's name to change it.\n\n• edit the time — click the total to type it (H:MM:SS, H:MM, or just minutes), or drag across it to scrub ±1 minute per step; the change is saved as a single correction.\n\n• forgot to stop? — once a task has run for over 8 hours, a gentle still-tracking row appears with its own stop button.\n\n• reorder — drag a row up or down to reorder the list.\n\n• {sym:xmark} delete — hover a row to reveal the ✕, click it, then confirm.\n\n• visible rows — in settings, cap the list to 3…15 rows (default 10); above the cap it scrolls, and the 8-hour warning stays pinned in view.\n\n• open a task — click a row to expand it: the full name, a description of your own, and a star for a favourite. settings can float starred tasks to the top.",
            .docTodosFull: "to-dos — a simple checklist.\n\n• add — click the + new task row, type, and press return.\n\n• check off — click the circle to complete a task; completed tasks sink to the bottom, dimmed and struck through. unchecking a task returns it to its place among the active ones.\n\n• reorder — drag a row to reorder; active and completed tasks each reorder within their own group.\n\n• {sym:xmark} delete — hover a row to reveal the ✕, click it, then confirm.\n\n• visible rows — in settings, cap the list to 3…15 rows (default 10); above the cap it scrolls, with the add row always in view.\n\n• open a task — click a row to expand it: the full text on the first line, a description under it, the icons below. return adds a line, ✓ or ⌘return saves, escape cancels.\n\n• remind — the bell sets a day and a time; the squares repeat it on the weekdays you pick. when it comes due you get a banner with snooze and done, a sound, and a mark in the menu bar — each one switchable in settings. a reminder that already went off leaves its time struck through in the list.\n\n• star — marks a favourite; settings can float starred tasks to the top.",
